{"toolCallId":"call_55e0919ce3c7496c878e0096f186ca8e","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"total 128\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   5257 26 Oct 14:48:22 2026 acceptance-criteria.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel    423 26 Oct 14:40:22 2026 description.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   5564 26 Oct 14:48:40 2026 graph-metadata.json\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   3682 26 Oct 14:44:38 2026 implementation-summary.md\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  14299 26 Oct 14:45:01 2026 plan.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 14:40:22 2026 scratch\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  10313 26 Oct 14:48:18 2026 spec.md\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  11393 26 Oct 14:48:20 2026 tasks.md\n--- grep new ids\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:61:| AC-008 | REQ-006 | Given a run that emits a warning on stderr, When `--quiet` is added, Then the warning is still written to stderr and stdout carries only the recommended-level line | `bash recommend-level.sh --quiet ... 2>stderr.txt >stdout.txt` leaves the warning in `stderr.txt` and `wc -l` reads 1 for `stdout.txt` | Unmet | - |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:52:- [ ] T014 Keep every stderr write on stderr in the quiet path, so a warning still reaches stderr when `--quiet` is set (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '2>' \"$S\"` prints nothing, and `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints nothing on a clean run (REQ-006).\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:114:| REQ-006 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so `--quiet` trims stdout only. |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree","termin