{"toolCallId":"call_65a4250e0efd42a0b015c7db6f98de57","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\nSpec Folder Validation v3.0.0\n\n  Folder: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n  Level:  3\n  Engine: orchestrator\n\n+ FILE_EXISTS: All required files present for Level 3\n! PLACEHOLDER_FILLED: 6 unfilled value token(s) in a Draft packet. Fill each one before the status leaves Draft\n    - implementation-summary.md:50: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Opening hook: 2-3 sentences on what changed and why it matters. Lead with impact.]\n    - implementation-summary.md:61: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Created/Modified/Deleted] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What this change accomplishe\n    - implementation-summary.md:70: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How was this tested, verified and shipped? What was the rollout approach?]\n    - implementation-summary.md:81: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What was decided] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Active-voice rationale with specific reasoning] |\n    - implementation-summary.md:92: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Validation, lint, tests, manual check] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: PASS/FAIL with specifics] |\n    - implementation-summary.md:101: 1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Limitation]** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Specific detail with workaround if one exists.]\n+ TEMPLATE_SOURCE: Template source headers present\n+ ANCHORS_VALID: Anchors well formed in 5 file(s)\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALID: Frontmatter continuity basics present\n+ FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK: All spec-doc frontmatter memory blocks are structurally valid\n+ SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY: All targeted spec-doc anchors meet the sufficiency baseline\n+ MERGE_LEGALITY: No merge plan supplied; legality check skipped\n+ CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION: No routing payload supplied; contamination check skipped\n+ POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT: No post-save payload supplied; fingerprint check skipped\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT: Graph metadata checked\nx GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY: Generated metadata integrity found 1 violation(s) (enforced)\n    - graph-metadata.json: SOURCE_FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH: source_fingerprint does not match a re-derive of the current source docs, the stored derived fields may be stale\nx GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT: Generated metadata drift found 1 drifted field(s) (enforced)\n    - description: stored 'Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh' drifted from fresh 'Every invocation of `recommend-level.sh` prints a 12-to-18-line text report: a level line, a score'\n+ COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER: No ephemeral comment-hygiene markers found\n+ SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED: Spec status is 'Draft', not Complete; scaffold markers are allowed\n+ STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY: status cross-doc check not applicable; one status is missing or unclassified\n    - spec.md Status=Draft classified=planned\n    - implementation-summary.md Status=<missing> classified=unknown\n+ AC_COVERAGE: Acceptance coverage gate not active for this level or lifecycle state\n+ TOC_POLICY: TOC policy passed: no TOC headings in non-research spec documents\n+ AI_PROTOCOLS: AI protocols present and complete (4/4)\n+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 3; phases=3, tasks=53, stories=3, scenarios=0)\n+ FOLDER_NAMING: Folder name '001-recommend-level-quiet-flag' follows naming convention\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALUES: Frontmatter values are in the shared list\n+ SOURCE_TAGS: No [SOURCE:] path:line citations in research or review artifacts\n+ GREP_CONVENTION: Grep convention: 5 document(s) conform\n+ LEVEL_MATCH: Level consistent across all files (Level 3)\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT: children_ids matches the on-disk phase children\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY: children_ids entries all carry the packet's own identity\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE: graph-metadata.json shape validation passed\n+ METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY: Generated metadata paths match on-disk folder: zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n+ DESCRIPTION_SHAPE: description.json shape validation passed\n+ NORMALIZER_LINT: No local normalizeScope*/getOptionalString declarations found outside allowed files\n+ SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY: Spec doc references, metadata, and handover targets resolve cleanly\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED: Canonical-save root-spec check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED: Canonical-save source-doc check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED: save_lineage is present for the refreshed graph metadata\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED: Packet identity is normalized across continuity, description, and graph surfaces\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS: Description and graph freshness stay within the canonical-save slack window\n+ CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS: Continuity freshness skipped: SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS is not enabled\n    - code:not_opted_in\n+ LINKS_VALID: All wikilinks under the system-spec-kit skill resolve\n\nSummary: Errors: 2  Warnings: 1\n\nRESULT: FAILED\n\nSome of these are recomputable from the repository. Fix them with:\n  node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag --apply\n  It rewrites generated metadata (description.json, graph-metadata.json), frontmatter packet\n  pointers and the Spec Folder row, and reports any failure it cannot repair. It never edits\n  other text. Run validate once after it.\n  Optional: run it without --apply first to preview the changes.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"2242e3","exit_code":2,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
