{"toolCallId":"call_d895fc51c7fd43dbbf391304789e3edc","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"189:> **Phase Parent Mode:** A spec folder is treated as a phase parent when at least one direct child matches `^[0-9]{3}-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` AND that child has `spec.md` OR `description.json`. Detection is implemented identically by `is_phase_parent()` (shell, in `runtime/cli/lib/shell-common.sh`) and `isPhaseParent()` (ESM JS, at `runtime/cli/dist/spec/is-phase-parent.js`). When detected, FILE_EXISTS skips Level-N file requirements at the parent and accepts only the lean trio. Phase children continue to follow their own Level 1/2/3/3+ contract. Tolerant policy: legacy phase parents that retain heavy docs continue to validate without churn.\n263:2. Run validation to confirm all requirements are met\n872:- level specifications reference - Documentation level requirements\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"347d18","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
