{"toolCallId":"call_e43ecc833ee243c492a82d9412aa398e","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: CHECK-AC-CLOSURE\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Sourced by validate.sh and compatible with strict mode.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Rule: AC_CLOSURE\n# Severity: error\n# Description: Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+.\n#   A packet may close when every criterion is Met, Waived or Superseded.\n#   Waived and Superseded rows must name a decision record that exists.\n#   Packets created before the rollout cutoff stay advisory on every branch.\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 1. INITIALIZATION\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n_acc_lower() {\n    printf '%s' \"$1\" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]'\n}\n\n_acc_numeric_level() {\n    printf '%s' \"$1\" | tr -cd '0-9'\n}\n\n# An unrecognised flag value enables the gate rather than disabling it: a\n# typo in an opt-out must not silently switch a closure gate off.\n_ACC_FLAG_NOTE=\"\"\n_acc_enabled() {\n    local raw=\"${SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE:-true}\"\n    case \"$(_acc_lower \"$raw\")\" in\n        true|1|yes|on) return 0 ;;\n        false|0|no|off) return 1 ;;\n        *)\n            _ACC_FLAG_NOTE=\"SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE='$raw' is not a boolean; the gate stayed enabled\"\n            return 0\n            ;;\n    esac\n}\n\n# Rollout boundary, overridable by operators. A malformed override falls back to\n# the default instead of being compared as a string, which would grandfather\n# every packet in the repository.\n_ACC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT=\"2026-08-30\"\n_ACC_CUTOFF_NOTE=\"\"\n_acc_cutoff_date() {\n    local raw=\"${SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF:-$_ACC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT}\"\n    local candidate=\"${raw:0:10}\"\n    if [[ \"$candidate\" =~ ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$ ]]; then\n        printf '%s' \"$candidate\"\n        return 0\n    fi\n    _ACC_CUTOFF_NOTE=\"SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF='$raw' is not an ISO date; using $_ACC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT\"\n    printf '%s' \"$_ACC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT\"\n}\n\n# Packet creation date from the spec.md metadata table. Matching is lowered\n# explicitly because the awk on this platform does not honour IGNORECASE.\n_acc_created_date() {\n    local spec_file=\"$1\"\n    [[ -f \"$spec_file\" ]] || return 1\n    local value\n    value=\"$(awk '\n        { line = tolower($0) }\n        line ~ /\\|[[:space:]]*\\*{0,2}created\\*{0,2}[[:space:]]*\\|/ {\n            if (match($0, /[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}/)) {\n                print substr($0, RSTART, RLENGTH)\n                exit\n            }\n        }\n    ' \"$spec_file\")\"\n    [[ -n \"$value\" ]] || return 1\n    printf '%s' \"$value\"\n}\n\n# Reads the Status CELL, never the whole row: a line-wide substring match reads\n# \"Not Complete\" and \"Blocked - nothing done yet\" as completion claims.\n_acc_completion_claimed() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local file status\n    for file in \"$folder/spec.md\" \"$folder/implementation-summary.md\"; do\n        [[ -f \"$file\" ]] || continue\n        status=\"$(awk -F'|' '\n            function norm(v) {\n                gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, \"\", v)\n                gsub(/\\*\\*|`|\\.$/, \"\", v)\n                gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, \"\", v)\n                return tolower(v)\n            }\n            /^[[:space:]]*\\|/ {\n                if (norm($2) == \"status\") { print norm($3); exit }\n            }\n        ' \"$file\")\"\n        case \"$status\" in\n            complete|completed|done|shipped|delivered|closed) return 0 ;;\n        esac\n    done\n    return 1\n}\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 2. TABLE PARSING\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Emits TAB-separated records. Columns are located by header name rather than by\n# position, so an escaped pipe or an extra column cannot shift the Status cell.\n# A row that looks like a criterion but does not parse is reported, never\n# skipped: a silently dropped row empties the table and closes the packet.\n_acc_rows() {\n    local ac_file=\"$1\"\n    awk '\n        function norm(v) {\n            gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, \"\", v)\n            gsub(/\\*\\*|`/, \"\", v)\n            gsub(/\\.$/, \"\", v)\n            gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, \"\", v)\n            return v\n        }\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"d42396","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_e9ec7720438d4356a6825e6422aa990c","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"check-ac-closure.sh\ncheck-ac-coverage.sh\ncheck-ai-protocols.sh\ncheck-canonical-save-description-graph-freshness.cjs\ncheck-canonical-save-description-graph-freshness.sh\ncheck-canonical-save-lineage.cjs\ncheck-canonical-save-lineage.sh\ncheck-canonical-save-packet-identity.cjs\ncheck-canonical-save-packet-identity.sh\ncheck-canonical-save-root-spec.cjs\ncheck-canonical-save-root-spec.sh\ncheck-canonical-save-shared.cjs\ncheck-canonical-save-source-docs.cjs\ncheck-canonical-save-source-docs.sh\ncheck-comment-hygiene.sh\ncheck-complexity.sh\ncheck-description-shape.sh\ncheck-files.sh\ncheck-folder-naming.sh\ncheck-frontmatter-values-helper.cjs\ncheck-frontmatter-values.sh\ncheck-frontmatter.sh\ncheck-graph-metadata-child-drift.sh\ncheck-graph-metadata-child-identity.sh\ncheck-graph-metadata-shape.sh\ncheck-graph-metadata.sh\ncheck-grep-convention-helper.mjs\ncheck-grep-convention.sh\ncheck-level-match.sh\ncheck-level.sh\ncheck-links.sh\ncheck-metadata-disk-consistency-helper.cjs\ncheck-metadata-disk-consistency.sh\ncheck-normalizer-lint.sh\ncheck-placeholders.sh\ncheck-scaffold-never-touched.sh\ncheck-source-tags-helper.mjs\ncheck-source-tags.sh\ncheck-spec-doc-integrity.sh\ncheck-status-cross-doc-consistency.sh\ncheck-template-source.sh\ncheck-toc-policy.sh\nREADME.md\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"f920f8","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_ea9596d633d84210be790d1ebbd58b5b","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"FILE_EXISTS | authored_template | error  | Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\nPLACEHOLDER_FILLED | authored_template | error  | Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\nCOMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER | authored_template | error  | Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\nSCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED | authored_template | error  | Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\nSTATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY | authored_template | error  | Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\nLEVEL_DECLARED | authored_template | info  | Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\nAC_COVERAGE | authored_template | info  | Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\nAC_CLOSURE | authored_template | error  | Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\nANCHORS_VALID | authored_template | error  | Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. A doc stamped v2.3 or later must also carry every anchor its template requires, meaning each section whose H2 header has no L2:, L3:, L3+: or FIX ADDENDUM: prefix, and each missing one is an error that names the doc, the anchor and the heading to restore. Template order is not checked.\nFRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK | authored_template | error  | Validates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\nMERGE_LEGALITY | operational_runtime | error  | Validates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\nSPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY | authored_template | error  | Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\nCROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION | operational_runtime | error  | Detects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\nPOST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT | operational_runtime | error  | Verifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\nTOC_POLICY | authored_template | error  | Enforces table-of-contents placement policy.\nAI_PROTOCOLS | authored_template | error  | Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\nCOMPLEXITY_MATCH | authored_template | error  | Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\nFOLDER_NAMING | authored_template | error  | Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\nFRONTMATTER_VALID | authored_template | error  | Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\nFRONTMATTER_VALUES | authored_template | warn  | Warns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list in sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json. Aliases are legal.\nSOURCE_TAGS | authored_template | warn  | Warns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or review artifacts names a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, using sk-doc's citation resolver. Packets created on or before the cutoff are skipped. A pass means the path and line exist, not that they support the claim.\nGREP_CONVENTION | authored_template | error  | Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\nLEVEL_MATCH | authored_template | error  | Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\nGRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT | operational_runtime | warn  | Checks generated description and graph metadata are present.\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT | operational_runtime | warn  | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY | structural | error  | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the packet's own current identity (stale rename residue the refresh writer now prunes).\nGRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE | structural | warn  | Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\nMETADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY | structural | error  | Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\nDESCRIPTION_SHAPE | structural | warn  | Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\nNORMALIZER_LINT | operational_runtime | error  | Strict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\nSPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY | authored_template | error  | Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\nTEMPLATE_SOURCE | authored_template | error  | Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED | operational_runtime | error  | Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED | operational_runtime | error  | Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED | operational_runtime | error  | Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED | operational_runtime | error  | Checks canonical save packet identity normalization.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS | operational_runtime | error  | Checks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\nCONTINUITY_FRESHNESS | operational_runtime | error strict | Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\nGENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY | structural | error strict | Validates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants, error under strict behind a grandfather report mode.\nGENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT | structural | error strict | Re-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and the current docs, read-only, error under strict only when the drift-gate flag is on and otherwise grandfather report mode.\nLINKS_VALID | operational_runtime | warn  | Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"833c8b","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_eeaa45ef0af445a59d44d7cd00522f59","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"61:RESULT: FAILED\n62-\n63-Some of these are recomputable from the repository. Fix them with:\n64-  node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag --apply\n65-  It rewrites generated metadata (description.json, graph-metadata.json), frontmatter packet\n66-  pointers and the Spec Folder row, and reports any failure it cannot repair. It never edits\n67-  other text. Run validate once after it.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"1ac900","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
